# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Intune Atlas .gitignore
# The point of most of these rules is to keep tenant data and secrets out of
# a public repo. Read SECURITY.md before committing anything exported from a
# tenant.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Raw tenant exports (unsanitized) ---------------------------------------
# Export into one of these locations, run the sanitizer, then commit only the
# sanitized copy under artifacts/.
exports/
export/
raw/
**/raw/
*.raw.json
*.unsanitized.json
*.export.json
*-export-*.json

# --- Secrets, tokens, certificates ------------------------------------------
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.snk
.env
.env.*
*.secret
*.token
*.credential
secrets.json
appsettings.*.json
config.local.*
*.local.ps1
*.local.psd1
*.local.json

# --- Device identifiers ------------------------------------------------------
# Autopilot hardware hashes and serial numbers are device secrets. Never commit.
*HWID*.csv
*hwid*.csv
*HardwareHash*.csv
*hardware-hash*.csv
AutopilotHWID*.csv
Autopilot*.csv
*serial*.csv

# --- Packaging output --------------------------------------------------------
*.intunewin
IntuneWinAppUtil.exe
*.msi
*.msix
*.msixbundle
*.appx
*.appxbundle
*.exe
*.dmg
*.pkg
*.apk
*.ipa
*.mobileconfig.signed

# --- Test and lint output ----------------------------------------------------
TestResults/
testResults.xml
*.TestResults.xml
coverage.xml
Pester-*.xml
PSScriptAnalyzer-*.xml

# --- OS and editor junk ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# --- Local scratch -----------------------------------------------------------
tmp/
temp/
scratch/
